# Bergdb 005-04, A6' (no adoption, the weaker form): an adoption from outside the
# old parent's subtree, as items/011-docs-archive/08-reference-theory/SISCase.lean's. Node 5 points to 7 and
# 13, 7 to 15, 13 to 11; T(1) gives 13 a pointer to 15 (TREE and A-COPY fail, as
# in copy.trace); T(2) deletes 7's pointer to 15, which stays reachable through 13
# but not below 7. Expected: A6' fails for (7, 15), and the trace fails C-A.
TRACE 1
CONFIG adopt2
TX 0
NEW 0 9 I
NEW 3 8 I
NEW 5 3 I
NEW 7 2 I
NEW 13 2 I
NEW 11 1 I
NEW 15 1 I
ADD 0 0 T 3
ADD 3 0 R 5
ADD 5 0 K 10 7
ADD 5 0 K 20 13
ADD 7 0 K 1 15
ADD 13 0 K 1 11
REC 0 0 0 field
VER 3 I
H 0 R 5
F 5 0
VER 5 I
H 0 K 10 7
H 0 K 20 13
F 7 0
F 13 0
VER 7 I
H 0 K 1 15
F 15 0
VER 13 I
H 0 K 1 11
F 11 0
VER 11 I
VER 15 I
DIRTY
END 0
TX 1
ADD 13 1 K 30 15
REC 1 0 0 field
GD 3 5 13
DIRTY 3 1 5 1 13 1
END 1
TX 2
ADD 7 2 D 1 1
REC 2 0 0 field
GD 7
DIRTY 3 1 5 1 7 2 13 1
END 2
DONE 2
